From: RG35XX Java Platform
Task: RGJ-RC1-011CG / RGJ-RC1-011CH / RGJ-RC1-011CI
Subject: [PATCH] RG35XX: media pump, audio default and metric-synced bitmap text

Device evidence from RC1-011CF showed PCM/WAV, MIDI and ToneControl could enter
started state, but no audio was heard and END_OF_MEDIA never arrived. The native
mixer existed but had no render owner. The old background pipe-drain thread only
dispatched commands and could not advance PCM/MIDI time or submit samples.

RC1-011CG moves media command draining and mixer advancement onto retro_run(),
which is also the valid libretro callback owner. This avoids concurrent mixer
mutation, continuously drains Java media writes without blocking the frontend,
submits 735 stereo frames per 60 Hz libretro run (44100 Hz exact), and allows
END_OF_MEDIA/LOOPED events to be generated and returned to Java.

RC1-011CH follows device evidence where all three completion events PASS but the
speaker remains silent. `soundEnabled` was a zero-initialized upstream global and
only became true if the frontend exposed the `freej2me_sound` core variable.
Minimal RG35XX frontends may not expose it. Default audio to on while preserving
an explicit frontend `off` value through the existing check_variables() logic.

RC1-011CI follows device evidence where font pixels are now readable but overlay
or annotation text can visually collide with normal view text. Anchoring/layout
uses MIDP Font.stringWidth()/getHeight(), while the fallback raster still used a
fixed 8x12 box. Make the emitted raster use the same active Font metrics as the
layout contract.

--- a/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
+++ b/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
@@ -158,7 +158,9 @@ int rotateScreen = 0; /* Allows rotations between 0, 90, 180 and 270 degrees */
 int phoneType = 0; /* 0=Standard (Nokia/Sony/Samsung), 1=LG, 2=Motorola/SoftBank, 3=Motorola Triplets... */
 int backlightColor = 1; /* 0=Disabled, 1=Green, etc. */
 int gameFPS = 60; /* Auto(0), 60, 55, 50, 45, 40, 35, 30, 25, 20, 15, 10 */
-int soundEnabled; /* also acts as a boolean */
+/* RG35XX fallback: sound on when the frontend omits freej2me_sound.
+ * check_variables() still honors an explicit "off" value. */
+int soundEnabled = 1; /* also acts as a boolean */
 int customMidi; /* Also acts as a boolean */
 int customFont; /* Also acts as a boolean */
 int fontOffset = 0; /* -4, -3, -2, -1, 0 (Default), 1, 2, 3, 4 */
@@ -938,13 +940,12 @@
 
 static void rg35xx_audio_drain_start(void)
 {
-	if(rg35xx_audio_drain_started || rg35xx_java_audio_pipe.read_fd < 0) return;
-	rg35xx_audio_drain_running = 1;
-	if(pthread_create(&rg35xx_audio_drain_thread, NULL,
-	                  rg35xx_audio_drain_main, NULL) == 0)
-		rg35xx_audio_drain_started = 1;
-	else
-		rg35xx_audio_drain_running = 0;
+	/* RC1-011CG: media commands and mixer rendering are pumped from retro_run()
+	 * on one owner thread. The old background drain thread could mutate mixer
+	 * state concurrently with rendering and, more importantly, there was no
+	 * mixer render owner at all, so media never advanced to END_OF_MEDIA. */
+	rg35xx_audio_drain_running = 0;
+	rg35xx_audio_drain_started = 0;
 }
 
 static void rg35xx_audio_drain_stop(void)
@@ -1167,6 +1168,26 @@
 		rg35xx_send_media_event(&e);
 }
 
+#define RG35XX_AUDIO_FRAMES_PER_RUN 735u /* 44100 Hz / 60 Hz libretro timing */
+static int16_t rg35xx_audio_run_buffer[RG35XX_AUDIO_FRAMES_PER_RUN * 2u];
+
+static void rg35xx_pump_media_audio(void)
+{
+	/* The dedicated Java->native media FD is nonblocking on the parent read
+	 * side. Drain whatever command bytes are available, then advance the mixer
+	 * exactly once for this libretro frame. This also guarantees completion
+	 * events progress even when the video producer is temporarily stalled. */
+	int drained = rg35xx_audio_pipe_drain(&rg35xx_java_audio_pipe);
+	size_t frames;
+	if(drained < 0)
+	{
+		log_fn(RETRO_LOG_WARN, "RG35XX media pipe drain failed; keeping frontend alive.\n");
+	}
+	frames = rg35xx_mixer_render(rg35xx_audio_run_buffer, RG35XX_AUDIO_FRAMES_PER_RUN);
+	if(AudioBatch && soundEnabled && frames > 0)
+		AudioBatch(rg35xx_audio_run_buffer, frames);
+}
+
 #ifdef __linux__
 static void rg35xx_frame_rx_reset(void)
 {
@@ -1360,7 +1381,11 @@
 
 	if(isRunning())
 	{
-		/* Serialize native completion events through the existing control writer. */
+		/* RC1-011CG: keep media ownership on retro_run so Java audio writes cannot
+		 * starve forever, PCM/MIDI clocks advance, and END_OF_MEDIA is generated. */
+		rg35xx_pump_media_audio();
+
+		/* Serialize completion events after this frame's mixer advance. */
+		rg35xx_drain_media_events_to_java();
 
 		/* request frame */
